-- title:
--   Uniqueness of the Ω-coordinate of lifts across square-zero thickenings
-- statement:
--   The setting is the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of a quaternionic ("fake elliptic curve") moduli problem. All of the following data are fixed.
--
--   **Base arithmetic data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$ (`hrr`) and a positive integer $N$ with $r \nmid N$, $\bar r \nmid N$ (`hrN`, `hrbarN`) and $N$ squarefree (`hN`). A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal{O}$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), with an irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`), $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`) and $(r) = (\pi)$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$. Further, an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $Onr$ which is a characteristic-zero domain, with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, such that $Onr$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal is maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr(x) \equiv x^r \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`); thus $Onr/\pi$ is an algebraic closure of the residue field and $Fr$ lifts its Frobenius. A homomorphism $vdet \colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively), characterised by `hvdet`: $vdet(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\pi^n$ for some $u \in \mathcal{O}^\times$.
--
--   **Quaternionic moduli data.** Rationals $a,b$ with `hB` asserting that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is indefinite ($0<a$ or $0<b$) and that for a finite place $v$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ the completion is a division algebra exactly when $v$ lies above $r$ or $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`). A scheme $\mathcal{X}$ with a structure morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ and a point assignment $pt$ taking fake elliptic curves of level $N$ over a ring $S$ to $\mathcal{X}$-points over $\operatorname{Spec} S$, with `h𝒳` asserting that this is a coarse moduli datum (invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, surjectivity and injectivity on geometric points, and the universal property). An integer $n \ge 3$ (`hn`) with $r \nmid n$, $\bar r \nmid n$ and $\gcd(n,N) = 1$ (`hrn`, `hrbarn`, `hnN`); a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ with point assignment $ptF$ on fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure, which `hM` asserts to be a fine moduli datum (isomorphism invariance, base-change compatibility, surjectivity and injectivity of $ptF$ on $S$-points for all $S$); a group $G$ acting by $\rho$ on $M$ with labels $\chi \colon G \to \Lambda$, `hρ` asserting that this action is a level-twisting action (each $\rho(h)$ lies over the structure morphism, twisting a level structure by $\chi(h)$ translates the $ptF$-point by $\rho(h)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, surjective and injective modulo $n$). A morphism $M \to \mathcal{X}$ over the base (`hp`), invariant under the $G$-action (`hρp`) and compatible with the two point assignments (`hp_pt`).
--
--   **Hecke and Atkin–Lehner data.** For every prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$ a scheme $\mathcal{Y}_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ with point assignment $ptT_\ell$ on curves with extra level $\ell$, a coarse moduli datum (`h𝒴`), together with two degeneracy morphisms $d_0,d_1 \colon \mathcal{Y}_\ell \to \mathcal{X}$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) realising on points the forgetful map (`hd₀`) and the $\ell$-isogeny quotient (`hd₁`). Endomorphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal{X}$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) realising the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **The definite quaternion side.** Rationals $a_1, b_1$ with `hdef` asserting $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in $\Lambda_1$ (`hΛ₁`, `hR₁`, `hRΛ₁`); an adelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) such that $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra embedding $\iota_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`); a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathbb{Z}$ containing $r$ (`hv`). A subgroup $\Gamma_t$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]^\times$ equal to the group of units integral at all places away from $v$ (`hΓt`); elements $s_\ell$ and adelic units $sf_\ell$ for each $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$ satisfying `hs` (four clauses: $sf_\ell$ is the diagonal image of $s_\ell$ away from $r$, is $1$ at $r$, the diagonal idele of $\ell$ times $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $\Lambda_1$ and $R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$); the groups $\Gamma_{t,\ell} = \Gamma_t \cap s_\ell \Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`); a unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **The reduction datum.** A hypothesis `hΛℤ` that all integers lie in $\Lambda$, and a coordinate map $coord \colon \Lambda \to \mathbb{Z}_{r^2}\times\mathbb{Z}_{r^2}$ which by `hcoord` is additive, sends $1$ to $(1,0)$, is multiplicative for the Frobenius-twisted product rule, is injective, has dense image, and is compatible with reduced traces. Over the residue ring $k_0 = Onr/\pi$: a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ of level $N$, a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ along the unit section of $A_0$, with `hA₀` asserting that $\theta_0$ identifies the formal completion of $A_0$ with $X_0$ compatibly with $coord$; endomorphisms $e(\gamma), e'(\gamma)$ of $A_0$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ with $e(\gamma)$ over the base (`he`) and degrees $\deg(\gamma)$. The clauses `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4` (summarised here) assert: $(e(\gamma),e'(\gamma))$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure; multiplicativity of $\gamma \mapsto e(\gamma)$ up to powers of $r$; rational scalars act by the corresponding multiplication up to powers of $r$, and conversely; on formal coordinates $e(\gamma)$ is induced by an element of the centraliser of the $X_0$-action whose matrix realisation is $r^{k_\gamma} g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$ for a single $g$; each full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$ is translated by $e(\gamma)$ by a label $lab(\gamma) \in \Lambda$, multiplicative and compatible with scalars modulo $n$; and every level-preserving self-isogeny of $r$-power degree of a geometric fibre of $A_0$ is, up to powers of $r$, induced by some $e(\gamma)$. An order $R_2 \subseteq R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`) with $r$-power denominators sufficing to reach $R_1$ (`hR₂r`), and endomorphisms $\hat e(x)$ of $A_0$ over the base for $x \in R_2$ (`hê`), subject to `hE5a`, `hE5b1`, `hE5b2`, `hE5b3`, `hE5c`, `hE5d`, `hE5e` (summarised here): additivity, $\Lambda$-equivariance and level preservation of $\hat e$; $\hat e(1) = \mathrm{id}$; multiplicativity; integers act by multiplication; $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x) = [\mathrm{nrd}\,x]$; agreement of $\hat e$ with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma_t$ up to powers of $r$; and a joint matrix normalisation of $e$ and $\hat e$ by a single $g$ as in `hE2`.
--
--   **The formal moduli datum.** A ring homomorphism $\iota \colon \mathbb{Z}_{r^2} \to Onr$; a special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $\Phi$ of height $4$ over $Onr/(r)$ (`hΦ`, `hΦ4`); a moduli package $MD$ over $Onr$ satisfying the Zariski sheaf condition (`hMD`); a map $\eta$ from rigidified formal modules to $MD$, with `hη` (three clauses): $\eta$ identifies admissible rigidifications exactly up to isomorphism, is natural in the base, and is locally surjective on a Zariski cover. A matrix realisation $E_0$ of the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action with `hE₀`: $E_0$ is injective and, for one exponent $m$, its image is exactly $r^{-m}M_2(\mathcal{O})$ in the two-sided sense stated. A comparison $eD$ between the functor $\mathcal{G}_{\mathcal{O}}(MD)$ on Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent and the product of the functor of $Onr$-algebra maps with Drinfeld's functor $\Omega_{K_0,\pi}$ of Deligne data, natural (`hnatD`), bijective on every such algebra (`hbijD`), preserving the leg coordinate (`hfstD`), intertwining the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on $MD$-points with the twisted action on $\Omega$-points (`hGLD`), carrying $\pi$-translation to the Frobenius twist of the leg (`hPiD`), and such that $\pi$-translates exist (`hPiexD`). A reduction map $\kappa \colon Onr/\pi \to Onr/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), and an isogeny $\beta_0$ from $\Phi$ to the reduction of $X_0$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`). A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$ over $k_0$.** A curve $A_{0w}$, morphisms $aw, aw', bw, bw'$ with the stated compatibilities over the base (`haw`, `haw'`, `hbw`, `habw`), an integer $kw$, the assertions that $(aw,aw')$ exhibits $A_{0w}$ as the Atkin–Lehner quotient of $A_0$ at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), that $(bw,bw')$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{kw}$ preserving the level (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw`, which adds to the conclusion of `hE2` that the composite $aw$ followed by $bw$ is, on formal coordinates, realised by an element whose matrix is $r^{k_w} g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$ for the same $g$.
--
--   **The uniformisation map.** An assignment $\Xi$ sending each rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, with leg $\psi \colon Onr \to B$, to a point of $\mathcal{G}_{\mathcal{O}}(MD)$ over $B$, subject to `hΞleg` (for $B$ with only trivial idempotents the leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (compatibility with pullback of curves and rigidifications), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves matching the auxiliary data up to powers of $r$) and `hΞdef` (an explicit description of $\Xi$ through $\eta$, a rigidified formal module transported by $\theta_0, \kappa, \beta_0$ with exponent $j \le 1$, admissible for the $(-j)$-th Frobenius twist of $\psi$). A matrix $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with `heqΓ` (translating a rigidification by $e(\gamma)$ moves $\Xi$ by the action of $r^c\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ for some $c$), `heqW` (the analogous statement for the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ and $\bar w$, when $\bar r$ is invertible in $B$), `hK1` (every Deligne datum over a $B$ with only trivial idempotents is attained, with the prescribed leg, by some rigidified curve, after the twisted action of $g_0^{-1}$), `hK2` (two such rigidified curves with the same Deligne datum are related by an isomorphism matching the rigidifications up to powers of $r$), `hK3` (the corresponding pullback existence along $\mathcal{O}$-algebra maps), `hK4` (lifting of rigidifications along a surjection whose kernel has square zero, together with the stated independence of the Deligne datum), and `hC0e`, `hC0u` (existence and uniqueness of the full level-$n$ structure transported from $P_0$ along a rigidification). Finally a map $\Theta_f$ which, for every Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, sends a triple consisting of an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\psi \colon Onr \to B$, a Deligne datum $P$ over $B$ and an element $g \in G$ to a $B$-point of $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$, natural in $B$ (`hΘnat`), whose value is computed by $ptF$ at the curve with transported level structure, post-composed with $\rho(g^{-1})$, whenever the data are compatible in the sense of `hΞ` and `hK` above (`hΘval`), and whose projection to $\mathcal{X}$ is $pt$ of the curve (`hΘvalc`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** For all Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebras $B$ and $B_0$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $B \to B_0$ (named `p` in the conclusion, not to be confused with the morphism $M \to \mathcal{X}$) which is surjective and whose kernel has square zero — stated as: any two elements of $B$ killed by it have product zero — every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\psi \colon Onr \to B$, every pair of Deligne data $P, P'$ over $B$ and every $g \in G$: if $P$ and $P'$ have the same image under base change along $B \to B_0$, and $\Theta_f$ takes the same value at $((\psi,P),g)$ and at $((\psi,P'),g)$, then $P = P'$.
--
--   The assertion is thus injectivity in the $\Omega$-coordinate alone: the leg $\psi$ and the group element $g$ are the same in the two arguments, and no connectedness assumption is imposed on $B$ in the conclusion (connectedness occurs only inside the assumed clauses `hΞleg`, `hΞdef`, `heqΓ`, `heqW`, `hK1`, `hK2`, `hC0e`).
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the formal étaleness of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation map $\Theta_f$ from the $\pi$-adic period functor to the formal neighbourhood of the quaternionic moduli scheme $M$: along a square-zero thickening, a lift of a Deligne datum is determined by its image point. It is obtained from the corresponding local statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.fineFamily_lift_unique_locally_of_value_of_squareZero`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.fineFamily_lift_unique_locally_of_value_of_squareZero) together with the gluing lemma [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.DeligneDatum.eq_of_forall_map_eq_of_span_eq_top`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.DeligneDatum.eq_of_forall_map_eq_of_span_eq_top) for Deligne data over a Zariski cover, and it is used by the existence statements for fine families, [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.fineFamily_exists_lift_of_value_of_squareZero_heightNormalised_conn`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.fineFamily_exists_lift_of_value_of_squareZero_heightNormalised_conn) and [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_fineFamily_of_evenRigidifiedPair_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_conn`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_fineFamily_of_evenRigidifiedPair_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_conn).
